and created one in the image of her son. And there's a kind of parallel with Cromwell, because who ultimately follows him? For a brief while, it's his son, but in the end, it's Charles II. And there's this kind of inability to really read the desires of the English people. So the English people, they'd let down Cromwell, they'd let down God, but worst of all, they'd let down themselves. I was about to say, they let down me.
